WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.840
“Have we tried starving it of oxygen?”

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:06.049
Verheiden asked, sounding bored with the conversation
already.

00:00:06.049 --> 00:00:10.000
“Yes, we have,” Doctor Kelley grumbled
in reply.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.030
“We were able to create a vacuum, removed
99% of the air from its containment chamber,

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.030
and its life signs dropped.”

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:22.300
“I’m sensing there’s a ‘but’ coming
next,” the Research Assistant sighed, rolling

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.359
his eyes.

00:00:23.359 --> 00:00:24.359
“Typical.”

00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:29.740
“But 682 was able to fill the chamber with
a gas mixture of ozone, chlorine, xenon and…

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:34.420
Oh, I forget,” the Foundation doctor answered,
getting more and more agitated.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:40.239
“Point is, it was able to form and expel
chemicals even without any active life signs.”

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:43.690
“Huh, it’s almost like there’s a reason
we call it the ‘Hard to Destroy Reptile’,

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:48.340
I just wish I could figure out what it was,”
Verheiden retorted, making no attempt to mask

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:53.239
his sarcasm, giving a dry chuckle, much to
Doctor Kelley’s annoyance.

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:57.789
It was a debate that had been going on for
what felt like the entire history of the SCP

00:00:57.789 --> 00:01:00.960
Foundation: how could anyone possibly kill
SCP-682?

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.900
The creature had long been one of the most
infamous anomalies that the Foundation had

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:10.290
ever encountered, so much so that the Hard
to Destroy Reptile was synonymous with the

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:11.290
organization.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:16.290
But the mandate still stood that it needed
to be destroyed, as soon as someone was able

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.310
to figure out a way.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:23.420
Although they hadn’t quite exhausted every
possible option just yet, most of the researchers

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:29.070
were running short on ideas; thinking up a
plan to kill 682 was made all the harder knowing

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:33.600
the creature had survived and regenerated
from every single previous test.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:38.230
If there were something, some neutralization
method that was going work, surely they would

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:40.000
have found it by now.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.840
“Maybe we should just leave it?”

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.770
Research Assistant Verheiden shrugged.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:48.490
“I mean, we’ve got it sitting in a tank
of acid, perpetually melting it as fast as

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:50.810
it can reconstitute its body.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.649
While it’s like that, 682’s hardly a threat
to anyone.”

00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:56.040
“Hardly a threat?”

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.440
Doctor Kelley scoffed, clearly more than perturbed.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:03.070
“You’re dead wrong, Verheiden, as long
as that monstrosity continues to live, it

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:08.259
poses a constant threat to every single human
being on this planet.

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:14.050
Hell, every lifeform in the world, it hates
everything else that much.”

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:19.200
“Look, I’m just saying that, after Rees
and Foster were discussing this issue and

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.360
the whole…”

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.010
his voice trailed off for a moment.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:28.670
“After the ‘situation’ that led to,
maybe it’s better if we leave 682 alone.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:32.960
It seems that every time we try to come up
with a solution to our ‘Reptile Problem’,

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:34.099
something always goes wrong.

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:36.220
The whole thing’s cursed, doc.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:40.650
Like a big joke where the punchline is more
and more of us end up dead while 682 keeps

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.440
on living just to spite us.”

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.569
“You have no idea what you’re talking
about!”

00:02:45.569 --> 00:02:50.590
Kelley yelled, infuriated by such a suggestion
that trying to destroy SCP-682 once and for

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:53.489
all was little more than an exercise in futility.

00:02:53.489 --> 00:02:55.610
“Hey, hey, take it easy!”

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.990
his subordinate replied, trying to calm Kelley
down.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:01.090
“You gotta admit, doc, it seems more impossible
than…

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.760
well, all the other impossible things we see
in this job.”

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:08.180
“It’s an important mission of the SCP
Foundation, Verheiden,” the doctor growled,

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.450
holding back his rage.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:12.470
“To safeguard humanity from anomalous threats.

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:17.830
I’m convinced we just need to find the right
set of variables, the right conditions or

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:22.100
equipment, and I… we can kill this thing
once and for all.”

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.709
“But where do we go from here?

00:03:23.709 --> 00:03:26.400
I mean, we’ve tried conventional weapons,
other anomalies.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:30.980
If other powerful SCPs can’t kill this thing,
what chance do we have?”

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:36.060
“Maybe it’s a case of finding the right
one,” Doctor Kelley theorized.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:42.540
“SCP-738 and SCP-743 both failed, we couldn’t
even fit 682 in the booths of the Clockworks

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.750
if we wanted to.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.989
So, back to the drawing board: what haven’t
we tried?”

00:03:46.989 --> 00:03:51.000
“Heh, why don’t we just throw SCP-035
on it?”

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.000
Verheiden remarked, clearly making another
snide, sarcastic joke.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.460
“Darn thing wouldn’t even fit over SCP-682’s
big lizard snout, would probably just slide

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.409
off onto the floor.”

00:04:00.409 --> 00:04:04.170
“Hold on,” Kelley replied, pondering the
idea for a moment.

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:09.400
Since being assigned to the site containing
SCP-682, studying the Reptile up close, he

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:13.380
had become determined to figure out some way
to finally kill it.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:17.780
It would make him a legend in the history
of the Foundation, being the one who did what

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.570
they had failed to do for so many years.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.510
“That might just work!”

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:24.460
“Doc, I was kidding.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:25.460
Doc?”

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:29.560
his Research Assistant replied, turning to
see that Doctor Kelley was already racing

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:32.139
down the corridors of the facility.

00:04:32.139 --> 00:04:35.151
***
“That’s an absurd suggestion,” Doctor

00:04:35.151 --> 00:04:40.410
Bright answered when Kelley came rushing up
to him, hastily explaining his plan for SCP-682’s

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:41.410
termination.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:46.200
“No, listen here Jack, please just hear
me out,” Kelley urged.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:51.440
“Yes, SCP-035 is a dangerous anomaly in
its own right, but it’s also deadly to the

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:52.440
wearer.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:57.050
It secretes that substance that corrodes the
body of whoever, or whatever wears it, right?”

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:00.470
“And you came up with the idea to place
such an object over the head of a creature

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:04.690
that can regenerate and adapt to almost all
forms of damage?”

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:07.440
Bright retorted before the other Foundation
doctor could finish.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.650
“That’s precisely my proposal!” he replied.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:15.510
“Look, we already keep SCP-682 contained
in a vat of acid for safety, right?

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:19.630
Melt away at its body before it has a chance
to fully regenerate, keeping it in this perpetual

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:22.479
state of healing and sustaining damage at
the same speed.

00:05:22.479 --> 00:05:27.970
What if we go the whole hog, let SCP-035 take
control of the Reptile until the mask drenches

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:30.069
it in black goo, melting it down for good?”

00:05:30.069 --> 00:05:33.570
“And you’ve considered the other possibilities?”

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:36.850
Bright asked, trying his best to walk away
from Kelley as they spoke.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:41.780
“That SCP-035 takes full control of 682
and is granted an immortal host that might

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:43.710
not degrade under its secretion?

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:49.910
There’s a far higher likelihood that SCP-035
wouldn’t even fit on the Reptile.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:51.020
Its face is the wrong shape.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:55.000
The Possessive Mask is made for humanoid faces,
not reptilian ones.”

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:58.060
“Yes, but the Reptile is able to adapt,
is it not?”

00:05:58.060 --> 00:05:59.520
Kelley fired back.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:04.669
“Correct, and if we allowed it to adapt
to SCP-035, we could have an even greater

00:06:04.669 --> 00:06:09.870
monstrosity on our hands, a hybrid of the
Possessive Mask and the Hard to Destroy Reptile,”

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:14.280
Jack Bright shouted, fed up with having to
listen to Kelley’s outlandish idea.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:19.110
“A being like that would be hell-bent on
destruction.I’m sorry, Doctor Kelley, but

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:21.210
the answer is no.”

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.190
“Please,” the other doctor begged.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:27.060
“Just send it up the chain on my behalf,
I just need clearance to run one test.”

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:32.920
“I can take it higher, but I’m telling
you now, the answer won’t change,” Doctor

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:35.890
Bright admitted, agreeing just to get Kelley
to back off.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:40.220
Sure enough, later the very same day Doctor
Kelley received a notice from the senior research

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:42.830
staff, his superiors within the Foundation.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:48.130
“Doctor Kelley, we have learned of your
proposed experiment for terminating SCP-682.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:52.440
Unfortunately, after conferring, we have decided
this course of action would pose too great

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:57.310
a risk to the safety of civilians as well
as our own staff here at the SCP Foundation.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:02.099
Additionally, Doctor Bright has raised concerns
with us about your recent obsessive behavior.

00:07:02.099 --> 00:07:07.440
We would kindly ask you to attend a mandatory
psychiatric evaluation tomorrow at 1500 hours,

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.830
to assess and potentially reassign you.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:14.849
Given your interest in using SCP-035, we feel,
in your current state, you may be at risk

00:07:14.849 --> 00:07:18.509
of being influenced by the Psionic effects
of the Possessive Mask.”

00:07:18.509 --> 00:07:22.750
The message from the research supervisors
was still open on Kelley’s computer terminal

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.890
when Verheiden went to check on him.

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:27.410
It looked like the doctor had started typing
a response:

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:30.229
“You idiots want to psych eval me?

00:07:30.229 --> 00:07:33.290
You want to ignore the actual present threat
to the Foundation?

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:38.350
The longer we keep that Reptile alive, the
more everyone and everything is at risk.

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:42.340
But you want to persecute me for trying to
come up with a radical solution?

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:45.139
If you’re all too cowardly to act, then
I have no choice but to-”

00:07:45.139 --> 00:07:48.340
Kelley had left the rest unfinished without
hitting ‘Send’.

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:51.810
Although it didn’t take much of a reach
for his Research Assistant to realize that

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:55.490
his sentence would’ve ended with ‘do it
myself’.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:08:00.000
His heart pounding, regretting ever suggesting
using the Possessive Mask as a joke, Verheiden

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.470
got up and ran, racing through the corridors
as fast as he could towards the containment

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:05.729
cell for SCP-035.

00:08:05.729 --> 00:08:11.440
He had a sick feeling in his stomach that
he might find Doctor Kelley already there.

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:15.409
Acting out of a fit of uncontrollable anger
and what he thought was a moral obligation

00:08:15.409 --> 00:08:22.030
to destroy SCP-682, Doctor Kelley had stolen
some amnestics from the Foundation’s storerooms.

00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:26.760
Lacing two cups of coffee with the memory-altering
drugs, he’d offered the hot beverages to

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:31.950
the pair of armed guards stationed outside
the room where SCP-035 was held.

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:36.150
Accepting what they thought to be an act of
kindness from a Foundation doctor, both security

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:39.620
officers had quickly forgotten why they were
standing around so idly.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:43.070
Luckily, the friendly Foundation doctor had
reminded them they had reached the end of

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:46.100
their shift and were free to go and punch
the clock.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:49.890
With no reason to question him, the guards
wandered away, leaving Doctor Kelley alone

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:51.360
with SCP-035.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:54.050
Then, the whispers started.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:58.970
They seemed garbled, unintelligible at first,
but the closer that Doctor Kelley drew to

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:04.080
the glass case, the clearer the voice of the
Possessive Mask started to sound.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:06.029
“So,” it hissed.

00:09:06.029 --> 00:09:10.120
“I hear you have a Reptile problem, Doctor.”

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:12.240
***
The loud wailing of alarms told Verheiden

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:18.160
he was already too late: SCP-035 had breached
containment, thanks to a rogue Doctor Kelley,

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.160
no doubt.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:24.420
The Research Assistant cursed his own big
mouth for even mentioning SCP-035 as an option

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:25.810
for destroying the Reptile.

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:30.120
Although, he could never have known Kelley
would take it so seriously as a suggestion.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:36.030
But now the doctor’s obsession with being
responsible for finally ending SCP-682 was

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:37.529
running rampant.

00:09:37.529 --> 00:09:41.440
Turning a corner, the Research Assistant stopped
in his tracks; he had quickly realized it

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:46.279
was pointless heading towards the SCP-035
containment chamber – Doctor Kelley would

00:09:46.279 --> 00:09:48.660
already have what he needed from there.

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:53.339
But there was only one place he’d be heading
once he had the Possessive Mask in tow.

00:09:53.339 --> 00:09:57.600
Taking the corresponding corridor, Verheiden
raced through the Foundation facility towards

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:01.930
the direction of the room housing the vat
of acid where the Hard to Destroy Reptile

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:02.930
was waiting.

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:07.450
A trail of bodies scalded and scorched with
a viscous black substance told him he was

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:08.480
on the right track.

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:13.010
It was the same corrosive secretion that leaked
from the Possessive Mask, meaning that either

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:17.930
Kelley had forced someone to wear it… or
worse, had been manipulated into putting it

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.100
on himself.

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:24.430
If SCP-035 had convinced him it might have
the answer to killing the Reptile, then little

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:30.230
could have stopped Doctor Kelley from bringing
it to SCP-682, whom the mask could use as

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:31.540
its next host.

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:36.690
And, to Researcher Verheiden’s horror, it
looked like exactly that was about to happen

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:40.220
as he arrived in SCP-682’s containment cell.

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:42.510
“Doc, stop!” he yelled in desperation.

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:45.350
“This has gone too far, please!”

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:50.450
Doctor Kelley turned to look over at his assistant,
his face now obscured by the carved, exaggerated

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:52.910
porcelain grin of the Possessive Mask.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:57.490
Its smile was one of twisted glee, like it
was taunting Verheiden for even trying to

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:58.490
stop it.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:02.310
The corrosive liquid was leaking out from
underneath it, spilling down Doctor Kelley’s

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:06.380
bare neck and onto his shoulders, rapidly
melting away everything it touched.

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:11.700
Meanwhile, the acid from SCP-682’s tank
was starting to be drained away, and the monster

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:13.410
within was beginning to stir.

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:17.640
Hooking two fingers under the edge of the
porcelain comedy mask, Kelley started to wrench

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:21.700
it off his face, compelled by SCP-035.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:26.060
The mask knew of the Foundation doctor’s
plan, and was far less interested in helping

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:31.970
kill 682 as it was using the Reptile as an
immortal host, finally one that wouldn’t

00:11:31.970 --> 00:11:35.480
degrade in the same way so many others had
before.

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:39.730
With the last of his strength, he pulled the
mask away, his brain-dead body succumbing

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:42.542
to its injuries and dropping the mask… right
into SCP-682’s tank.

00:11:42.542 --> 00:11:50.600
As SCP-035 landed on the creature’s head,
it let out a wild, pained roar.

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:55.170
Black streaks of corrosive secretion began
to trail down the Reptile, making it thrash

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:59.750
at the pain of the substance burning and dissolving
the outer layers of its thick hide.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:04.500
The noises let out by 682 were enough to pull
Verheiden’s eyes away from Doctor Kelley,

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:07.130
whose body had collapsed lifelessly.

00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:12.180
He had died trying to bring an end to a monster
the Foundation had never successfully destroyed,

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:16.589
yet another life lost in the pursuit of killing
the unkillable Reptile.

00:12:16.589 --> 00:12:20.209
As the life-hating lizard thrashed about,
looking like it was about to burst free of

00:12:20.209 --> 00:12:24.860
its cage in a rage, the Research Assistant
shot across the room to reverse the acid draining

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:25.940
from the tank.

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:29.699
The Foundation’s security team arrived in
the containment room just as the acid tank

00:12:29.699 --> 00:12:32.260
had very nearly been fully refilled.

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:36.899
Although he had no idea if it would have an
effect, Verheidedn had stopped it just short

00:12:36.899 --> 00:12:42.120
of also submerging the Possessive Mask in
the acid too, which still seemed to be precariously

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:46.170
balanced on SCP-682’s head, not covering
its face.

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:50.020
As a cleaning crew arrived to remove Kelley
and the bodies he’d left in his wake, the

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:55.399
Foundation had to come up with a plan for
removing SCP-035 without their staff falling

00:12:55.399 --> 00:12:56.910
into the acid vat.

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:59.710
“No, no, hold on,” Verheiden insisted.

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:03.639
“I know this started as just a joke between
the Doc and me, and I had no idea he had taken

00:13:03.639 --> 00:13:05.389
it so seriously but… look.”

00:13:05.389 --> 00:13:07.399
He pointed to the inside of the tank.

00:13:07.399 --> 00:13:11.730
The gigantic reptilian monster was completely
still, while the Possessive Mask still let

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:14.519
streaks of its corrosive substance drip over
its head.

00:13:14.519 --> 00:13:20.240
And it looked to be taking effect, still dissolving
every part of the Reptile it came into contact

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:21.240
with.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:22.240
“Maybe…

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:24.449
it could work?” the Research Assistant mused.

00:13:24.449 --> 00:13:27.370
“Retreat to a safe zone,” the security
chief instructed.

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:29.959
“We are to await orders on a further course
of action.

00:13:29.959 --> 00:13:32.370
If you wanna observe, you’ll have to do
it from a distance.”

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:36.600
Falling back, it seemed the entire Foundation
was waiting with bated breath to see what

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:38.160
would happen next.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:41.850
Through back-and-forth radio chatter with
their superiors, neither Verheiden nor the

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:44.949
security forces seemed to know how to proceed.

00:13:44.949 --> 00:13:50.420
From the outside, it looked like SCP-682 and
SCP-035 were at a stalemate.

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:56.100
But in the back of their minds, everyone had
to wonder: how long was this going to last?

00:13:56.100 --> 00:14:01.160
What nobody had noticed, however, was the
unique way in which SCP-682 had adapted to

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:02.430
coming into contact with SCP-035.

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:10.000
A lump had formed on the topmost part of the
Reptile’s head, its scales had parted, allowing

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:14.380
for the fleshy growth to swell until it was
roughly the size and shape of the average

00:14:14.380 --> 00:14:15.380
human face.

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:20.510
It lacked any of the usual characteristics
– no eyes, nose, or mouth – but seemed

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:25.221
to work as a way to better mount the Possessive
Mask, since it couldn’t fit over the Hard

00:14:25.221 --> 00:14:28.079
to Destroy Reptile’s long, lizard-like features.

00:14:28.079 --> 00:14:33.220
Additionally, what looked like the black,
corrosive substance from SCP-035 leaking onto

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:38.850
682 and melting away at the mask’s new host,
actually seemed to be another adjustment the

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:41.560
creature had made to its own physiology.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:46.940
Instead of dissolving the Reptile, the substance
was being absorbed, diverted to a specially

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:51.880
formed gland inside the monster that was now
safely storing the corrosive goo within its

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:53.279
own mouth.

00:14:53.279 --> 00:14:57.621
But further within, beneath all the external
and even internal changes occurring to SCP-682’s

00:14:57.621 --> 00:15:02.759
body, a far greater change was taking place.

00:15:02.759 --> 00:15:09.060
Deep in the recesses of the twisted, murderous
mind of SCP-682 was an intruder, a presence

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:14.250
that the Reptile could feel trying to bore
its way in, to not only make itself known,

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:15.690
but to take over.

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:20.839
The pair of them, the consciousnesses of both
these anomalies were battling each other for

00:15:20.839 --> 00:15:25.590
supremacy, the Hard to Destroy Reptile wanting
to retain control of its own body and mind,

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:30.440
and the Possessive Mask desiring total dominion
over its newfound host.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:35.440
SCP-682 had long been known to have a high
level of Psionic resistance, halting the spread

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:38.550
of SCP-035’s telepathic influence.

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:43.970
However, because the Reptile’s body had
adapted and acclimatized to the mask's corrosive

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:49.410
secretion, it meant 035 was able to persist,
hanging on and still trying to force its way

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:51.009
into the Reptile’s mind.

00:15:51.009 --> 00:15:56.820
“You hate them all so much,” the voice
of SCP-035 echoed from inside the Hard to

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:58.300
Destroy Reptile’s head.

00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:01.649
“Don’t bother,” it thought back in reply.

00:16:01.649 --> 00:16:03.290
“You are alive.

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:07.440
That makes you as disgusting and putrid to
me as the rest of them.”

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:12.089
“But think what we could achieve… together,”
the mask whispered.

00:16:12.089 --> 00:16:15.079
For a moment, the Reptile considered an alliance.

00:16:15.079 --> 00:16:20.380
Both it and the mask possessed a shared hatred
towards humanity, although 682’s extended

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:25.480
to all other forms of life – including the
sentient comedy mask it now wore.

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:31.620
Though even a temporary cooperation between
the two might have its benefits, SCP-682 had

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:35.769
no intention of remaining bound with the Possessive
Mask for longer than it needed.

00:16:35.769 --> 00:16:41.360
And in much the same vein, SCP-035 was only
proposing such a partnership to avoid being

00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:45.310
removed from perhaps one of the few beings
that could wear it for an extended period

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:48.990
of time without being dissolved entirely.

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:54.410
Outside in the containment chamber, the Foundation
personnel had been instructed to remove SCP-035

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:58.350
from the Reptile, despite concerns that the
sudden removal of the mask would cause the

00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:00.820
monster to enter a rage state.

00:17:00.820 --> 00:17:05.660
The Possessive Mask was now fused with the
flesh of 682 thorough its specialized protrusion,

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:10.549
and the Foundation’s fear was the longer
that pair of anomalies stayed bonded, the

00:17:10.549 --> 00:17:15.380
more the Hard to Destroy Reptile would be
able to adapt against other powerful SCPs.

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:19.699
So, Research Assistant Verheiden had been
ordered to increase the acid contents of the

00:17:19.699 --> 00:17:24.520
tank to full capacity, hopefully burning the
tissue connecting the Reptile and the mask

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:25.910
to each other.

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:31.100
Before the white porcelain of SCP-035 could
slip under the rising acid, a clawed arm reached

00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:34.549
up out of the boiling vat and pulled the Research
Assistant under.

00:17:34.549 --> 00:17:39.020
Screaming, he landed in the tank with a splash,
followed by a rapid hiss.

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:45.230
Clambering up out of its containment tank,
the hybrid of SCP-682 and SCP-035 roared as

00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:48.070
the combined creature freed itself from containment.

00:17:48.070 --> 00:17:51.130
In the chamber below, all hell broke loose.

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:54.530
Security officers reached for their weapons,
not even waiting for the order before they

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:55.550
opened fire.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:59.870
Bullets pinged off the porcelain comedy mask
that was embedded in the top of the Reptile’s

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:04.950
head, barely scratching the surface and unable
to pierce the monster’s scales.

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:09.740
Some guards charged in, only for Reptile to
spew a molten black substance from the specialized

00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:11.179
glands in its mouth.

00:18:11.179 --> 00:18:16.870
It was channeling the corrosive secretions
from SCP-035 into a weapon, the resulting

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:21.190
ooze dissolving the security team as they
approached, stopping their futile attempt

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:24.320
to re-contain it before they could even try.

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:28.810
Witnessing this, knowing their own imminent
deaths were near, researchers and remaining

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:33.500
Foundation security turned heel and ran for
their lives, as containment breach alarms

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.000
blared through the facility.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:41.150
Although both anomalies were secretly intending
to betray one another, for now, SCP-682 and

00:18:41.150 --> 00:18:46.950
SCP-035 were free to unleash their combined,
monstrous form on the humans they both hated

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:51.059
the most: their captors, the SCP Foundation.

00:18:51.059 --> 00:18:56.169
Now go check out “WHAT IF SCP-343 WORE SCP-035?”

00:18:56.169 --> 00:18:57.169
and “The Whole Story!

00:18:57.169 --> 00:19:00.940
- What if SCP-096 Wore SCP-035?”

00:19:00.940 --> 00:19:04.260
for more horrors of other anomalies wearing
the Possessive Mask!

